## TCP/IP Model

Also known as the Internet Protocol Suite Model.

### Layer 1: Link Layer (Network Access)
- Combines OSI Layers 1 & 2
- Hardware addressing
- Physical transmission

### Layer 2: Internet Layer
- IP addressing and routing
- Corresponds to OSI Layer 3
- Protocols: IP, ICMP, IGMP, ARP

### Layer 3: Transport Layer
- Corresponds to OSI Layer 4
- TCP (reliable) and UDP (unreliable)
- Port numbers (0-65535)

### Layer 4: Application Layer
- Corresponds to OSI Layers 5, 6, 7
- User applications and services
- Examples: HTTP, SMTP, FTP, Telnet, SSH, DNS

