## VLAN & Trunking

### What is a VLAN?

Virtual Local Area Network - logically separates networks on same physical switch.

**Benefits:**
- Increases security
- Reduces broadcast traffic
- Improves performance
- Easier network management
- Flexibility in network design

### VLAN Types

#### Data VLAN
- Carries user traffic (default VLAN 1)
- Usually VLAN 2-1005

#### Management VLAN
- For administrative access to switch
- Enables remote management

#### Voice VLAN
- Dedicated for VoIP traffic
- Separate from data for QoS

#### Native VLAN
- Untagged VLAN on trunk port
- Default is VLAN 1
- Should be changed for security

### VLAN ID Range

| Range | Type |
|-------|------|
| 1 | Default VLAN |
| 2-1005 | Standard range (stored in flash) |
| 1006-4094 | Extended range (requires specific switch models) |
| 4095 | Reserved |

### 802.1Q Trunking

**Purpose:** Allows multiple VLANs across single link

**How it works:**
1. Switch adds 4-byte VLAN tag to frame
2. Tag contains:
   - Priority (3 bits)
   - CFI (1 bit)
   - VLAN ID (12 bits)
3. Receiving switch reads tag and forwards to appropriate VLAN

**Exception:** Native VLAN traffic sent untagged

### Trunk Port Configuration

#### Manual
```
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 1,10,20,30
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk native vlan 99
```

#### Dynamic Desirable (DTP)
- Initiates negotiation to become trunk
- Can become access or trunk port

#### Dynamic Auto (DTP)
- Responds to negotiation requests
- Can become access or trunk port

### Access Port Configuration

```
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode access
Switch(config-if)# switchport access vlan 10
```

### VLAN Configuration

```
Switch(config)# vlan 10
Switch(config-vlan)# name Sales
Switch(config-vlan)# exit

Switch(config)# interface vlan 10
Switch(config-if)# ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
```

### Inter-VLAN Routing

**Methods:**
1. Router with multiple interfaces (traditional)
2. Router on a Stick (single interface, subinterfaces)
3. Layer 3 switch (modern approach)

#### Router on a Stick

```
Router(config)# interface g0/0.10
Router(config-subif)# encapsulation dot1Q 10
Router(config-subif)# ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0

Router(config)# interface g0/0.20
Router(config-subif)# encapsulation dot1Q 20
Router(config-subif)# ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
```

