## Wireless Networking

### Wireless Standards

| Standard | Band | Speed | Range |
|----------|------|-------|-------|
| 802.11a | 5 GHz | 54 Mbps | ~35 m |
| 802.11b | 2.4 GHz | 11 Mbps | ~38 m |
| 802.11g | 2.4 GHz | 54 Mbps | ~38 m |
| 802.11n | 2.4/5 GHz | 600 Mbps | ~70 m |
| 802.11ac (WiFi 5) | 5 GHz | 3.5 Gbps | ~50 m |
| 802.11ax (WiFi 6) | 2.4/5/6 GHz | 10+ Gbps | ~50 m |

### Wireless Security

#### Open
- No authentication
- No encryption
- Insecure

#### WEP (Wired Equivalent Privacy)
- Weak encryption (40/104-bit)
- Outdated
- Easy to crack

#### WPA (WiFi Protected Access)
- Improved WEP
- TKIP encryption
- Still vulnerable

#### WPA2
- Strong encryption (AES)
- Current standard
- Supports PSK and Enterprise modes

#### WPA3
- Latest security standard
- Stronger encryption
- Protection against brute-force attacks

### Wireless LAN Configuration

#### Ad-hoc Mode
- Peer-to-peer devices
- No AP required
- Limited range

#### Infrastructure Mode
- Devices connect through AP
- Centralized
- Better range and performance

### SSID (Service Set Identifier)
- Network name
- Broadcast or hidden
- Max 32 characters

### Channel Selection

**2.4 GHz Band:**
- 11 channels available
- Channels 1, 6, 11 are non-overlapping (USA)
- Interference if channels overlap

**5 GHz Band:**
- Many more channels
- Less interference
- Higher data rates
- Shorter range

